+# Classic method profile
+
+The original five phases, Run, lock, transactions and `agent.continuation` remain authoritative. `/comet` is the user entry; these bindings add no stage commands or second progress ledger. TeamAI distributes assets only.
+
+## Managed qualification
+
+The sole current optional profile ID is `comet-managed-v2`; its canonical DATA is `foundation/profiles/comet-managed.json`. The filename is not another profile alias. Read the current profile and pinned method manifest in the project. A source installation does not enable this profile. Until the protected launcher, executor, result provenance and gates are qualified, the result is UNQUALIFIED. Missing method, executor, identity or binding fails closed; never use unmanaged defaults, a role label, or retired methods as fallback.
+
+Only Comet chooses and dispatches an action and accepts its outcome. Continue from the existing Runtime state/continuation; do not invent CLI commands, write phase/ACL, create a second Goal/scheduler, or turn a method into a controller. A method read or matching hash proves source selection, not application or independent acceptance. Runtime binding and gate enforcement remain separately qualified construction dependencies.
+
+## Bindings inside the same Run
+
+| Native phase / logical action | Method and independent output |
+| --- | --- |
+| Open / R | Requirements author uses unmodified grill-me, reuses confirmed decisions and authorized knowledge; writes OpenSpec goal, scope and AC. R confirmation precedes architecture. |
+| Design / A | Architecture author uses grill-me and writes current design/ADR. Independent multi-agent-consensus-review uses the protected quorum/threshold and the unchanged current artifact; preserve original manifest, ballots, tally/finalize. No copied or re-bound votes. |
+| Design / T | test-authoring produces cases, meaningful oracles, coverage, environment and cleanup. A distinct semantic test-design reviewer must pass T; structure alone and author self-check never pass it. |
+| Build / P | Plan author consumes only the planner protocol export below. Same OpenSpec tasks/DAG, original IDs; no dispatch, Goal, monitor or archive contract. |
+| Build / tests and implementation | test-authoring owns executable tests and fixtures. Builder uses Matt tdd (real cause-matched RED then GREEN), diagnosing-bugs when needed. Independent code-review retains Standards and Spec review. |
+| Verify / V | Independent whitebox-verify uses the actual candidate, typed ledger, validator and business terminal readback. The verifier cannot repair product/tests and sign its own acceptance. |
+| Archive / Kp, spec, Kt | Required LLMWiki project knowledge and independent index/reference readback precede every archive entry; only the Comet Spec Adapter archives OpenSpec. Outline team publication may resume after archive in the same Run and blocks overall completion until its fixed UUID/revision/audience is read back under current authorization. |
+
+R, A and T are separate gates, not extra phases. Failed or stale evidence returns through Comet to its owning author/adapter. Requirements/design changes invalidate all downstream evidence, including after old bytes are restored. These are obligations for qualified runtime gates, not proof that this source package implements them.
+
+## Planner protocol export (P only)
+
+From the unchanged claude-parallel-tdd-planner snapshot, read only `references/plan-contract.md` sections `One root and acceptance source` and `DAG` (stop before `Execution contract`). The pure `scripts/plan_guard.py` may validate the current plan. Do not load SKILL.md, automation/parallel-execution/execution-prompt/completion/openspec-closeout references, render_execution_prompt.py or openspec_lifecycle.py. Those belong to the full controller and cannot be activated inside a product Run. The raw snapshot is retained intact for provenance; this allowlist does not edit it.
+
+## Missing dependencies
+
+Report the actual missing capability and UNQUALIFIED, keeping the same pending Run. Installing these Comet assets, testing fixtures, reading a method or printing success never authorizes managed enablement, trusted roles, publication or completion. Preserve user-owned methods and old Run data. Legacy `subagent-driven-development` / `executing-plans` values are native strategy tokens only; `docs/superpowers` and `<classic-superpowers-root>` are compatible physical paths, not executable dependencies.
